  "readout": {
    "readout_answer": "27",
    "readout_text": "To determine how many miles from City A Alicia and Beth will meet, we analyze the situation using the concept of relative motion.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Understand the Setup**\n\n- **Distance between City A and City B:** 45 miles  \n- **Alicia's speed:** 18 miles per hour (from A to B)  \n- **Beth's speed:** 12 miles per hour (from B to A)  \n- **Both start at the same time and move toward each other.**\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Calculate the Time Until They Meet**\n\nSince they are moving toward each other, their **relative speed** is the sum of their individual speeds:\n\n$$\n\\text{Relative speed} = 18 \\text{ mph} + 12 \\text{ mph} = 30 \\text{ mph}\n$$\n\nThe time it takes for them to meet is the total distance divided by their relative speed:\n\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{45 \\text{ miles}}{30 \\text{ mph}} = 1.5 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Calculate the Distance from City A**\n\nAlicia is traveling from City A at 18 mph. In 1.5 hours, the distance she covers is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Distance from A} = 18 \\text{ mph} \\times 1.5 \\text{ hours} = 27 \\text{ miles}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Final Answer**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{27}\n$$\n\nThey will meet **27 miles from City A**.",
